The one-colour marks in logos/ -- BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Cloud Storage, Google
Cloud, Google Maps, dbt, Redshift, S3, MySQL, Snowflake, ClickHouse, Kafka,
SQS, Spark, Polars, DuckDB, Airflow, Terraform, Kubernetes, Docker and Bash --
come from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), whose SVG files are released
under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

CC0 covers the files, not the marks. Each is a trademark of its owner; they
are drawn here to say which service a step or a stream connects to, and that
use implies no endorsement. Some owners publish their own guidelines for
showing their marks (Google Cloud and dbt Labs among them), and those apply.

The breve in logos/brevissql.svg is Brevis's own mark (docs/BRAND.md).
